  "note": "Two questions per collection. relevant_ids are the point ids that would let a scholar answer the question. topic_ids are the point ids that are on the subject of the question. Both were curated by reading the passage text of a dense retrieval run. The gap between the two is the point: for the four collections that still hold a 10k sample, the subject is often missing from the corpus, so the strict set is empty and the topic set is thin. That is a corpus finding, not a harness bug. acceptable_intents lists the intents that may legitimately serve the question. A hadith question that is really a ruling question may go to fiqh, and a question about the Hijra may go to Seerah as well as to history.",
